{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","title":"Chain rule intuition"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A composition is a two-stage machine. First square x and add one; then cube the result. At x equals one, follow the values.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Chain rule: linked rates"},{"op":"equation","id":"functions","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"u=x^2+1,\\qquad y=u^3"},{"op":"diagram","id":"chain","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"text","at":[0.12,0.3],"content":"x = 1"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.5,0.3],"content":"u = 2"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.88,0.3],"content":"y = 8"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.24,0.3],[0.38,0.3]],"stroke":"solid","arrow":true,"label":"inner"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.62,0.3],[0.76,0.3]],"stroke":"solid","arrow":true,"label":"outer"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Near x equals one, a tiny change in x produces about twice that change in u. The first stage has local multiplier two.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"inner_rate","anchor":{"el":"functions","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\left.\\frac{du}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=\\left.2x\\right|_{x=1}=2"},{"op":"arrow","id":"first_rate","canvas_id":"chain","from":[0.12,0.46],"to":[0.5,0.46],"stroke":"solid","label":"×2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At u equals two, the cubing stage multiplies tiny changes by twelve. What multiplier results when both stages act in sequence?","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"outer_rate","anchor":{"el":"inner_rate","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\left.\\frac{dy}{du}\\right|_{u=2}=3(2)^2=12"},{"op":"arrow","id":"second_rate","canvas_id":"chain","from":[0.5,0.46],"to":[0.88,0.46],"stroke":"solid","label":"×12"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What is the combined local multiplier from x to y?","expected_gist":"Multiply the local multipliers: 2 times 12 equals 24."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5a835204-d022-4f2d-a929-9dd024a6677c","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The local multipliers multiply: two times twelve gives twenty-four. The chain rule multiplies the outer derivative by the inner derivative, evaluated at their corresponding inputs.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"combined","canvas_id":"chain","from":[0.12,0.68],"to":[0.88,0.68],"stroke":"solid","label":"×24 locally"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"outer_rate","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy}{du}\\frac{du}{dx}=3(x^2+1)^2\\cdot2x"},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=12\\cdot2=24"}],"checkpoint":null}}
